module contract;

// librdkafka topic-partition list ordering — resource-projection vocabulary
// version 1.
//
// Card W37-CORPUS-CONTRACTS-4. ONE TRUSTED ASSUMPTION about one upstream
// function. This module verifies nothing: the C body is not analyzed by this
// loader, and a declaration is a premise.
//
// Read from the pinned checkout at Fluent Bit
// 66910c10a4d7eafa810b84229cf2dcf7b0f26f97 on this card's own run.
//
// ## Why this callee
//
// `rd_kafka_topic_partition_list_sort` is the SOLE blocker of TWO projected
// functions, the highest function-cover yield of any callee this card could
// honestly declare:
//
//   * `rd_kafka_topic_partition_list_sort_by_topic`
//     (`lib/librdkafka-2.15.0/src/rdkafka_partition.c:3675-3680`)
//   * `rd_kafka_topic_partition_list_sort_by_topic_id` (`:3682-3687`)
//
// ## The body, read from `lib/librdkafka-2.15.0/src/rdkafka_partition.c:3664-3674`
//
//     void rd_kafka_topic_partition_list_sort(
//         rd_kafka_topic_partition_list_t *rktparlist,
//         int (*cmp)(const void *, const void *, void *),
//         void *opaque) {
//
//             if (!cmp)
//                     cmp = rd_kafka_topic_partition_cmp_opaque;
//
//             rd_qsort_r(rktparlist->elems, rktparlist->cnt,
//                        sizeof(*rktparlist->elems), cmp, opaque);
//     }
//
//   * `rktparlist` is READ (`->elems`, `->cnt`) and its element array is
//     PERMUTED IN PLACE by `rd_qsort_r`. Nothing is allocated, nothing is
//     freed, no element is removed, and the list is not stored anywhere that
//     outlives the call. Reordering an array does not change who owns it: the
//     caller's obligation to `rd_kafka_topic_partition_list_destroy` the list
//     is exactly what it was before the call, which is what `resource_borrowed`
//     says.
//   * `cmp` is a FUNCTION POINTER, projected `fnptr` — the mode and spelling
//     `msgpack/packer.qcore` already uses for `msgpack_packer_init`'s
//     `callback`. It is called, never freed, and carries no custody. The
//     `if (!cmp)` default substitution is a local rebinding of the parameter
//     and is invisible to the caller.
//   * `opaque` is a `void *` passed straight through to `cmp` as its third
//     argument. This body neither dereferences nor frees it; whatever the
//     comparator does with it is the comparator's business, and the caller's
//     custody of it is unchanged across THIS call. Borrowed.
//   * The result is `void`, so `resource_return_none()` is the faithful — and
//     the only faithful — result mode.
//   * `cmp` is explicitly NULL-guarded, so this body tolerates a null
//     comparator. Nothing here asserts non-nullness of any parameter, and a
//     borrowed declaration installs no entry resource, so no failure path is
//     deleted — the hazard constraint 4 names.
//
// ## Sorting is not custody, and that is the point
//
// The two target functions each pass a NAMED comparator and `NULL`:
//
//     rd_kafka_topic_partition_list_sort(rktparlist,
//                                        rd_kafka_topic_partition_cmp_opaque, NULL);
//
// so the interesting question is whether the permutation can disturb the
// resource identities the projection tracks for the list's elements. It cannot,
// because the elements are tracked through the LIST, not through an index: a
// sort moves values within an array the caller still owns whole, and this
// projection's unit of custody is the `rd_kafka_topic_partition_list_t *`.
// Recorded because it is the premise a reader would want stated rather than
// assumed.
//
// ## The duty gate (constraint 8)
//
// The body is defined in `lib/librdkafka-2.15.0/src/rdkafka_partition.c`, which
// IS one of the 185 analysed units (161 projected functions in the baseline)
// and which also contains BOTH target functions, so the duty gate applies with
// full force. This declaration is the NEUTRAL ELEMENT — every formal
// `Borrowed`, result `None` — the weakest statement the vocabulary can make
// (constraint 4's `N(m)`), so a derived summary can contradict it only by
// claiming a formal is released, transferred, delivered or restored. This body
// performs no such operation on any parameter.
//
// The body's own call to `rd_qsort_r` is uncontracted, so W4 may derive no
// summary for it at all — and "absence of evidence is not evidence": nothing is
// withdrawn on a body W4 derives no summary for. Should a conflict arise it is
// a `SummaryConflict` diagnostic with the declaration governing, never a silent
// override, and a withdrawal would be scoped to `rdkafka_partition.c` alone.
//
// ## ABI (constraint 8)
//
//     lib/librdkafka-2.15.0/src/rdkafka.h:1163
//         RD_EXPORT void rd_kafka_topic_partition_list_sort(
//             rd_kafka_topic_partition_list_t *rktparlist,
//             int (*cmp)(const void *a, const void *b, void *cmp_opaque),
//             void *cmp_opaque);
//
// One definition in the whole tree, external linkage. `RD_EXPORT` is a
// visibility decoration changing no type, arity or calling convention.
// `rd_kafka_topic_partition_list_t *` and `void *` are each one object-pointer
// level, `ptr<mut, u8>`; the function-pointer parameter is `fnptr`; the `void`
// result is `unit`. Arity is three, as declared. The header spells the third
// parameter `cmp_opaque` where the definition spells it `opaque`; a
// declaration's parameter NAMES are its own, and this module follows the
// DEFINITION's spelling with the disagreement recorded here rather than
// silently resolved.
//
// ## NOT CLAIMED
//
//   * Nothing about the ordering the comparator imposes, its consistency, its
//     stability, or whether `rd_qsort_r` sorts correctly.
//   * Nothing about `opaque`'s validity, or about what the comparator does with
//     it. A comparator that frees something through `opaque` would be a custody
//     effect this declaration does not model and does not exclude — recorded as
//     `RDKAFKA-SORT-COMPARATOR-EFFECTS`.
//   * Nothing about thread safety; a concurrent mutation of the list during the
//     sort is a data race this projection neither models nor excludes.
//
// ## Read at the same time and DELIBERATELY LEFT UNDECLARED
//
//   * `rd_kafka_topic_partition_destroy0` (`:2970`) has the next-highest
//     function-cover yield in this unit (two functions) and is DELIBERATELY NOT
//     declared, on two independent grounds published in this card's report: it
//     is `static` with no header declaration and is defined in the very unit
//     that calls it, so W4 is the correct lever; and it is a CONDITIONAL
//     release (`if (do_free) rd_free(rktpar);`) whose five other call sites in
//     this unit pass `do_free == 0`, so a `released` declaration would be false
//     at those sites and would move in the admitting direction.
//   * `rd_kafka_topic_partition_cmp_opaque`, `rd_kafka_topic_partition_by_id_cmp_opaque`
//     and `rd_qsort_r` are named by these bodies and block no projected
//     function in the baseline.

// ## Re-declared: the comparator is no longer read as benign
//
// Card CG22-CALLBACK-REGISTRY-CONTRACT (contract spec C04.19, gateway rules
// 13u, 13z). The declaration above read `cmp` as `resource_borrowed` and left
// what the comparator does to the caller's state unstated
// (`RDKAFKA-SORT-COMPARATOR-EFFECTS`): its two callers were `Safe` by assuming
// the comparator benign, which the card's rule forbids. `rd_qsort_r` calls
// `cmp(a, b, opaque)` during the call only, zero or more times, with two
// pointers into the list's element array and the caller's `opaque`:
// `resource_callback_invoked(cmp, _, _, opaque)`. A caller is now decided by
// the comparator's own contract (rule 13u), so both callers, whose
// comparators (`rd_kafka_topic_partition_cmp_opaque`,
// `rd_kafka_topic_partition_by_id_cmp_opaque`) have no contract in force, are
// `Unknown` (named corrections in the card's report). The body rebinds `cmp`
// (the `NULL` default) and hands it on to `rd_qsort_r` rather than calling it,
// so rule 13y's check does not validate it and the declaration is withdrawn in
// `rdkafka_partition.c` (every call there refuses, `callback-withdrawn`); a
// `NULL` actual is an open set wherever the declaration stands. The body is
// byte-identical at `66910c10` and `046accf6`.

// --- the in-place ordering of a topic-partition list ---
extern fn rd_kafka_topic_partition_list_sort(rktparlist: ptr<mut, u8>, cmp: fnptr, opaque: ptr<mut, u8>) -> unit
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(rktparlist);
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(cmp);
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(opaque);
    ensures normal resource_callback_invoked(cmp, _, _, opaque);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};
